user_prompt:
Bind chart evidence to each item in recon_diff_package.diff_items, using chart_canonical_package.excerpts[] (excerpt_id, section, text) and coder_facts_package (services, labs, immunizations, and evidence_refs per fact) as your evidence sources, governed by evidence_binding_options.

Deterministic-first binding rules (apply before considering any LLM-style fallback):
- Immunization administration and products (code_base in {90460, 90461}): support evidence = S3 services.immunizations.administered_events[].evidence_refs, plus counseling narrative evidence refs if used for 90460 eligibility; contra evidence = excerpts indicating 'not given', 'declined', 'refused' (pattern scan). If vaccine product codes are present, support evidence = administered_events lines containing the vaccine string (given-by).
- Labs / POC tests / specimen collection: support evidence = S3 labs performed evidence refs (e.g., result lines); contra evidence = pattern 'to be performed', 'ordered', 'plan', without a result/performed status. For code_base in {36415, 36416}: support evidence = capillary triggers ('Hemoglobin, Capillary', 'capillary', 'fingerstick', 'heel stick') or venipuncture triggers ('venipuncture', 'phlebotomy', 'venous blood').
- E/M codes (code_base 99xxx, preventive 99381-99397 or problem E/M 99202-99215): support evidence = S3 encounter type, reason for visit, HPI/ROS/Exam/Vitals excerpts, and age/DOB evidence refs for preventive mapping; no typical contra evidence — instead mark binding_confidence=inconclusive if only templated sections exist.
- Quality codes: support evidence only if S3 explicitly captured a measured action/result; contra evidence if the action is stated as planned only.

Fallback (LLM-style) evidence binding — invoke ONLY when evidence_binding_options.llm_fallback_enabled is true AND the deterministic binder returns fewer than 2 support refs AND the code_base is not in an excluded family AND the excerpt corpus is sufficiently bounded. When it applies, pre-filter excerpts by section tags and keyword hits for the code_base family (top ~30-60 excerpts) and return support_evidence_refs[], contra_evidence_refs[], binding_confidence (strong|moderate|weak|inconclusive), and binding_notes. Set binding_method to 'llm_fallback' when this path is used, otherwise 'deterministic'.

Validations: every support_evidence_refs[]/contra_evidence_refs[] entry must exist in chart_canonical_package.excerpts; if evidence_binding_options.include_snippets is true, snippet arrays must align to refs (same order, same count) and must not exceed the configured max refs per item; reject and warn (EVIDENCE_NOT_FOUND) on any excerpt ID that does not exist rather than fabricating one.

Return ONLY this JSON object (no markdown, no extra text):
{
  "recon_evidence_package": {
    "document_id": "doc_...",
    "evidence_binding_options": {
      "deterministic_first": true,
      "llm_fallback_enabled": true,
      "max_support_refs_per_item": 5,
      "max_contra_refs_per_item": 5,
      "include_snippets": true
    },
    "diff_items_enriched": [
      {
        "diff_id": "d_0001",
        "diff_type": "AI_ONLY|HUMAN_ONLY|MISMATCH_UNITS",
        "impact_class": "UNDERBILL|OVERBILL|DENIAL_RISK|QUALITY_GAP|NEUTRAL",
        "line_ref": {
          "line_type": "BILLABLE|QUALITY",
          "coding_system": "CPT_I|CPT_II|HCPCS",
          "code_base": "",
          "modifier": ""
        },
        "ai_group": {
          "indexes": [],
          "units_list": [],
          "units_total": 0
        },
        "human_group": {
          "indexes": [],
          "units_list": [],
          "units_total": 0
        },
        "support_evidence_refs": [],
        "contra_evidence_refs": [],
        "support_snippets": [],
        "contra_snippets": [],
        "binding_method": "deterministic|llm_fallback",
        "binding_confidence": "strong|moderate|weak|inconclusive",
        "binding_notes": ""
      }
    ],
    "warnings": [
      {
        "warning_code": "EVIDENCE_NOT_FOUND|LLM_FALLBACK_DISABLED|EXCERPT_CORPUS_TOO_LARGE",
        "message": "",
        "diff_id": "d_0001"
      }
    ]
  }
}

